nakula,
(1) (m.; cf. next; = AMg. ṇaula), a kind of musical instrument: LV 〔163.6〕; 〔206.14〕; 〔212.4〕; Mv 〔ii.159.4〕; 〔iii.407.19〕; all prose; Tib. transliterates;
(2) n. of a gandharva: Suv 〔162.4〕.

Nakṣatrarāja,
(1) n. of three former Buddhas: Mv 〔i.137.14〕; 〔iii.231.9 f.〕; Śikṣ 〔9.1〕; n. of a Buddha in the zenith: Sukh 〔98.14〕;
(2) n. of a Bodhisattva: SP 〔3.9〕.
